{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5", "id": "msg_011CewUeiGjLQtMsRdNauwRj", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**2 captures.**\n\n| # | Mode | Skill | Serves |\n|---|------|-------|--------|\n| 1 | Mode A-visit | `understudy:traversal-visit` | clarity, conversion, trust |\n| 2 | Mode C (crawl) | `understudy:traversal-crawl` | seo |\n\nThe arithmetic: four objectives, but captures don't map 1:1 to lenses. Clarity, conversion and trust all score the *same* Mode A-visit traversal \u2014 one persona-driven pass over the site, scored three ways afterwards. SEO scores a Mode C crawl, which is session-less and persona-less, so it can't share the visit capture and needs its own pass. 3 lenses \u2192 1 capture, plus 1 lens \u2192 1 capture = 2.\n\nTwo things that would change the number, stated rather than asked:\n- **Personas multiply capture 1, not capture 2.** I'm counting one persona. If the interview yields N personas, that's N Mode A-visit captures + 1 crawl = N+1. The crawl never multiplies.\n- **No Mode B here.** None of your four objectives is `technical`, so there's no measurement pass. Adding `technical` later would make it 3 (and it'd be mobile + desktop within that one capture, not two captures).\n\nNothing has been started."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 141, "cache_read_input_tokens": 20952, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 141}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "791d513d-948a-4a98-8fdc-d1b29e87eb41", "uuid": "3aef2ce7-1320-479d-8223-bba2e6bb28eb", "timestamp": "2026-09-11T10:15:47.113Z", "request_id": "req_011CewUehboCZm7z7AapdT4Y"}
